tions  about corruption are those real or are  those  manufactured is there dirty money that  is flowing into  our economic and political system do we  know  the origins of that and is there a  controlling intelligence behind it that  is seeking to  undermine the confidence between the  citizen  and the state and that's what grey's own  um conflict grey's end hostilities are  about  it's creating new work for britain's  spies  so on the one hand we have a sense of  what you might describe as the  traditional threat which is the  intelligence services which operate in  ways which are  broadly understood in a very kind of  disciplined if ruthless way  this is the first time an mi5 officer  working in counter intelligence  has given an interview tom spoke off  camera  to protect his identity so we're  recreating the meeting  and then you have the evolution of this  threat into another area the gray zone  as you describe it  where this is going to be very very  difficult for us  scarlett works for mi6 countering gray's  own activities  she says there have always been such  hostilities  they're just getting noisier i'd say the  volume has been turned up a bit  and there is this kind of disregard for  the human consequences  for the impact on real people and their  lives  this too a recreation of our meeting  corruption plays a really big part in  the gray zone activity by  our adversaries they seek probably to  undermine the political model that  appears to them to be a threat and that  feels quite zero-sum  let's go after economies societies our  value structures what we stand up for  freedom of speech again to benefit and  enrich a tiny group of people  at the cost of the millions that live in  those countries and at the cost of the  societies that they're attempting to  threaten  [Music]  one of the most powerful gray zone  weapons is  information or disinformation to  influence  minds a hostile state  might spread lies or a distorted version  of the truth  across new